{
  "source": "Hand-typed development starter. WHO International Nonproprietary Names (INN) and their common dosage forms only. NOT a licensed drug database, NOT a national formulary, and NOT verified against a regulator's register — every entry carries lastVerifiedAt: null so the app labels it 'not verified against a source'.",
  "notes": [
    "WHY THERE ARE NO BRAND NAMES OR MANUFACTURERS HERE.",
    "",
    "A brand-to-manufacturer mapping is a factual claim about a specific",
    "company's product on a specific market. We have no licensed source for",
    "those, and CLAUDE.md forbids generating drug facts and storing them as",
    "reference data. Typing plausible ones would produce a catalogue that looks",
    "authoritative and is not - which is worse than an empty catalogue, because",
    "a doctor would reasonably assume someone checked it.",
    "",
    "So the starter carries INN generic names and dosage forms, which are",
    "public, non-proprietary, and stable. Brand rows enter the catalogue when a",
    "licensed dataset is integrated (source_kind LICENSED_IMPORT), or one at a",
    "time as DOCTOR_CONTRIBUTED. Until then a doctor types the brand they mean",
    "into My Medicines, which is exactly what the personal library is for and is",
    "never blocked by what the catalogue does or does not contain.",
    "",
    "Two markets are present to prove the schema is not Bangladesh-shaped. The",
    "same molecule appears once per market, as it would in any real catalogue."
  ],
